      en: "Mondorf-les-Bains is a renowned spa town in southeastern Luxembourg, famous for its thermal springs and luxurious ambiance. The town's history took a decisive turn in 1841 when thermal water was accidentally discovered during test drilling for salt. Since then, Mondorf has developed into a center for wellness and health, attracting visitors from all over Europe. Another unique feature of the commune is Casino 2000, the only gambling casino in the Grand Duchy of Luxembourg, which is also a significant venue for cultural events and fine dining. The extensive spa park with its manicured gardens, sculptures, and historic pavilions provides an ideal environment for relaxation and leisurely walks. Aviation enthusiasts can visit the Luxembourg Aviation Museum, housed in a historic building within the town. Mondorf-les-Bains maintains a charming, sophisticated character, combining medical tradition with modern entertainment. Its proximity to the French border and the picturesque surroundings make it one of the country's most exclusive destinations.",
